jlens-cli is an unofficial command-line wrapper for the Jacobian lens.
It is not affiliated with or endorsed by Anthropic.

Version 0.2 consolidates the agent-friendly wrapper from
https://github.com/dirtycomputer/j-lens-cli
at de94a22b519742236aa90e3bfa7162228a0cbc7c.
Wrapper copyright: Copyright 2026 Xinyuan Wang; Apache-2.0.
The source repository history is retained in the consolidation merge.

Upstream: https://github.com/anthropics/jacobian-lens
Pinned commit: 581d398613e5602a5af361e1c34d3a92ea82ba8e
Upstream copyright: Copyright 2026 Anthropic PBC
Upstream license: Apache License, Version 2.0

The upstream numerical implementation and visualization assets are installed
as a dependency, not copied into this repository. Model/lens presets are
adapted from the upstream walkthrough notebook.

The jpplens / j-lens++ commands are an independent compatible reader for the
published merged checkpoints at https://huggingface.co/koayon/jpp-lenses
(Apache-2.0). No checkpoint weights or J++ training code are bundled.
J++ attribution: Kola Ayonrinde and Jack Lindsey, "J++ Lens: Jacobian Filtering
Enables More Faithful Workspace Lenses", 2026.
The reader applies the documented final-norm/LM-head readout using the pinned
Anthropic Jacobian lens inference engine. It is not the official workspace_lens
package, and does not implement J++ clustering, LRP fitting or expert weighting.
